1. This file contains the instruction to 
run prescribed soil moisture experiments with CAM5 with the same setups as in Teng et al. 2019

2. tag:
I used cesm1_1_2_LENS_n16, but sorry I can't find this tag from cseg/collections any more.
The source code that I used (/glade/p/cgd/ccr/people/hteng/CAM5.ctrl/model/cesm1_1_2_LENS_n16) was deleted. Fortunately,
I can find a copy from /glade/p/cgd/cas/asphilli/cesm_tags/cesm1_1_2_LENS_n16. 
To avoid losing it again, i made a copy at /glade/work/hteng/hteng/soil/cesm1_1_2_LENS_n16.tar.


3. workflow
3a: extend the control run: f.e11.F1850C5CN.f09_f09.001
(http://www.cesm.ucar.edu/experiments/cesm1.1/LE/)
(hpss: http://www.cesm.ucar.edu/experiments/cesm1.1/LE/)


two purposes:
i. we need 100 restart files. e.g. if you want to start your ensemble on 11-01, you'll need to extend the control from 01-01 to the end of oct.
ii. the original f.e11.F1850C5CN.f09_f09.001 doesn't provide daily U/V/T/Z etc.  that you will look at. 

(sorry I didn't save my 05-01, 06-01, 07-01, 08-01, 11-01, etc. restart files.)
but for your reference, you can look at my script:
/glade/work/hteng/hteng/soil/bin/rerunctrl.csh

a small tip: I usually write the script to set up member01, compile it, then make a soft link for other 99 cases to save time


3b: prescribed soil moisture runs
use /glade/work/hteng/hteng/soil/bin/PJun0_lev1-2_1mon.csh 
as an example (deplete soil water in the Great plains box) 


step0: setup member01  
you can follow /glade/work/hteng/hteng/soil/bin/PJun0_lev1-2_1mon.csh,just run member01.
run the command mannually till "./cesm_setup".
then copy the restart files.

the sourcemods are located at /glade/work/hteng/hteng/soil/sourcemods, you can ignore
*.F90.old, *.F90.corrected, *.F90.nopres and *.F90.liqonly
  
step1:   
create the soil moisture climo file with the ncl /glade/work/hteng/hteng/soil/ncl/new/P0_lev1-2.ncl.
the domain is defined by blat, elat, blon and elon
it creates a mask file /glade/work/hteng/hteng/soil/forcing/P0_lev1-2.nc
inside blat,blon,elat,elon, 
h2osoi_liq(ff,:,idomain)  =  0.0000001,
h2osoi_ice(ff,:,idomain)  =  0.0000001
or you can set it to a prescribed value.

step2:
edit user_nl_clm at caseroot: 
/glade/work/hteng/hteng/soil/dom21/PJun0_lev1-2_1mon-01/user_nl_clm 
copy user_nl_cam, user_nl_cice

for reference, you can look at PJun0_lev1-2_1mon.csh:
cp {$myhome}/namelist/user_nl_clm_P0_lev1-2  ${caseroot}/user_nl_clm 
cp {$myhome}/namelist/user_nl_cam ${caseroot}
cp {$myhome}/namelist/user_nl_cice $caseroot
rm -f {$caseroot}/CaseDocs/docn.streams.txt.prescribed
chmod 664 {$caseroot}/Buildconf/docnconf/docn.streams.txt.prescribed  
cp $myhome/namelist/user_docn.streams.txt.prescribed $caseroot 


step3
./*.build, build the case interactively


step4
run member01

step5
if member01 is successful, create member02,03,...100, use a softlink for the executable to avoid compiling each case.


